WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.200
We're at the Masna border crossing,

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.960
the crossing point between Lebanon and Syria.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.160
A Babel Doc Pro

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.240
There's been non-stop crossfire here for a week.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.640
On one side of the border,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.720
there are people who have been trying to flee the country since the regime change.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.280
They are Shiites,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.240
Alawites and Christians.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.720
They are religious minorities and they are afraid,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.000
convinced that the sunny Islamists,

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.680
the new masters of Damascus,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:33.880
will come after them.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.040
I can speak to terrorists,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.040
but they don't allow us to go inside

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.360
Lebanon. If you stay here,

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.760
what will happen?

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:48.200
I don't know.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.000
I will pay all my money.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.760
But I don't know what I'm going to do.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.040
Now I am going to Syria to kill me.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.360
On the other side of the border,

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.320
there are the people returning to Syria after years of exile.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:06.600
Like Basma,

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.600
who was a refugee in Beirut with her daughter and her granddaughter just a few months old.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.000
She's a businesswoman who runs two dental practices.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.240
I can't believe that after all this time
I can cross this border.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.800
It's my first time in 14 years!

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.920
Unlike some people, I've never been back.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.240
I couldn't go back as long as
Bashar al-Assad was there.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.480
As of December 2024,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:38.360
6 million Syrians have fled their country since 2011 and the start of the civil war.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:39.840
Like Basma,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.560
a student in Damascus.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.440
She took part in a demonstration against the dictatorship.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.000
She risked imprisonment for doing so,

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.680
so she chose to flee.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:50.560
For her,

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.840
this return is a historic day.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.800
All along the road,

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.240
there are remnants of the rout of the regime.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.880
We have suffered so much
and today there is nothing but joy.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:16.560
I breathe in freedom and there's nothing
more precious on this earth.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:23.920
It's better than the taste of bread
and better than anything!

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.920
We are free.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.160
We are free for the first time.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:36.320
May God protect us.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.440
O Lord.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.320
Two hours later,

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:40.440
Damascus,

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.440
and the first memories come flooding back.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.600
That's the area where I was studying.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:55.600
I was just starting my studies.
It's right here.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.960
My country, my Syria.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.000
But how dare they take it away from us?
My God.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:09.040
My God, how dare they deprive us of our own country.
My God. But how is that possible?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:16.960
Al-hamdu li-l-lah, Al-hamdu li-l-lah.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:32.640
On this day she finds the capital rejoicing and she's going back to the neighborhood of her childhood where she grew up where

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:42.320
she'll find her younger sister her nieces and her cousin who've planned everything to welcome her a PA system in the street and party music

