4x4s that were used to transport regime officials.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:59.520
The Assad family fortune is estimated to be between 1 and 2 billion dollars.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.200
How did the clan get so rich?

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:11.120
It all began in 1970,

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:13.240
when General Hafez al-Assad,

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.280
Bashar's father,

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.920
seized power in Syria in a military coup.

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:21.880
He overthrew a fragile democracy that had been established nine years earlier.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:26.640
My dear compatriots, greetings.
Thank you for listening.

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:29.960
Hafez al-Assad established a hardline dictatorship.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.320
Opponents were arrested,

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:32.880
Islamists targeted,

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:35.120
only one political party was allowed,

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:36.600
and the press was muzzled.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:40.560
The Ba'ath Party leader held Syrian society in an iron grip.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:48.000
What characterises this regime is ultra-violence,
permanent terror.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:51.200
All Syrians speak,
and have always spoken, of fear.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.240
This repression,
particularly of the Muslim Brotherhood,

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:59.760
but also of the left-wing opposition that also existed
in Syria, culminated in 1982 in Hama.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:03.920
There were aerial bombardments,
massacres, atrocities, disappearances.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.520
God is great.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.120
Many foreign heads of state attended his funeral.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:36.920
Jacques Chirac was the only Western president.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.520
They came to greet the new Syrian head of state,

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:41.560
Hafez's son,

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:42.680
Bachar al-Assad,

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.280
taking the place of his brother,

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:46.520
who had died suddenly in a car accident.

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:53.200
God, Syria and Bashar.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:20:01.440
The son, Bashar, who at the time was specialising
in ophthalmology in London, was called home urgently.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:09.280
So he was someone who, on the face of it, was
not at all prepared to take over from his father.

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.360
a priori,

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:18.400
was not at all prepared to take the succession of his father.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:28.880
His wife had grown up in England. So she helped
to develop an image of Syria as opening up.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.000
Throughout their reign,

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:34.600
Bashar and Asma al-Assad put their private life on show,

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:37.000
presenting themselves as a modern couple.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.880
This new image of Syria won admiration from diplomats everywhere.

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:43.440
From Russia to Iran,

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.400
Bashar al-Assad became an important interlocutor.

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.160
He was received by every head of state.

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:51.440
SYRIAN ARAB REPUBLIC

00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:57.440
I have always been convinced that,
while respecting its traditional alliances,

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:01.840
Syria could make a contribution to peace.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:47.040
Criminal, we hate you.
Get out, you and your regime!

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.240
I'm not in the hospital.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:55.680
Our souls, our blood for freedom.
Our souls, our blood for freedom.

00:22:00.480 --> 00:22:03.120
My brother, they've killed my brother!

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:09.680
By the end of 2011, 8,000 people had already
disappeared into the regime's jails.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:15.440
This dual system of intelligence services
and prison system is truly characteristic

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:17.680
of the regime of Bashar al-Assad

00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:24.320
and his father and sets the Assad regime apart,
if you like, from other dictatorships in the region.

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:37.680
...the regime of al-Assad compared to other dictatorships in the region.

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:44.160
So there was no order to make any attack.

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:46.040
We don't have any chemical weapons.

00:22:46.600 --> 00:22:48.360
We gave up our arsenals few years ago.

00:22:48.920 --> 00:22:49.720
Even if we had them,

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:51.280
we wouldn't use them.

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:57.320
And we have never used our chemical arsenal in our history.

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:12.160
In my opinion, what characterises this regime
is the violence, the capture of national wealth,

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:16.720
and the total absence of limits to the use of repression.

00:23:16.880 --> 00:23:22.080
Hundreds of thousands have died,
probably 600,000 in the 13 years of war.

00:23:24.080 --> 00:23:24.760
Mass murder,

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:25.800
embezzlement,

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:26.560
corruption,

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:28.440
but also drug trafficking.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:32.600
The family has also turned its country into a drug dealing state.

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:40.560
The state has been criminalised,
under Bashar al-Assad specifically.

00:23:40.800 --> 00:23:48.320
We know about the regime's role in drug trafficking,
first when it occupied part of Lebanon,

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:56.160
and now trafficking, captagon and so on.
It is a regime that has made itself criminal.

00:24:03.320 --> 00:24:04.240
In this warehouse,

00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:06.600
thousands of bags were awaiting shipment.

00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:09.200
Inside were pills of Captagon,

00:24:09.680 --> 00:24:12.760
a psychostimulant nicknamed the poor man's cocaine.

00:24:15.920 --> 00:24:16.160
5KVA

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:17.280
SVC
5 KV/

00:24:17.280 --> 00:24:17.520
