00:24:24.640 --> 00:24:28.960
The Syrian state earned between 7 and 10 billion dollars from this trade.

00:24:31.480 --> 00:24:34.440
The trafficking was controlled by Bashar al-Assad's brother,

00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:35.840
Maher al-Assad,

00:24:36.320 --> 00:24:37.560
shown here in the background.

00:24:41.840 --> 00:24:47.280
Abu Muhammad al-Jolani has committed to putting an end to it and to destroying all stocks.

00:24:49.960 --> 00:24:51.760
To celebrate Syria's new beginning,

00:24:51.960 --> 00:24:57.480
the masters of Damascus have called on all the country's Muslims to unite at the Great Friday Prayer.

00:24:57.520 --> 00:24:58.360
On that day,

00:24:58.400 --> 00:24:59.040
for the first time,

00:24:59.040 --> 00:25:00.000
the Muslims of Damascus have been able to get together.

00:25:00.080 --> 00:25:00.920
In 50 years,

00:25:01.280 --> 00:25:04.480
they will no longer be celebrating the glory of the Assad's.

00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:14.560
I want a flag too!
Give me some money for a flag!

00:25:16.200 --> 00:25:19.120
30-year-old Razan wouldn't miss this moment for the world.

00:25:19.360 --> 00:25:22.480
She's going with her two sisters to the great mosque of Damascus,

00:25:22.840 --> 00:25:25.640
the religious heart of Syria for 14 centuries.

00:25:26.080 --> 00:25:29.200
Today is all about joy and freedom.

00:25:29.360 --> 00:25:35.120
Today is the day of rebirth, it's a great day,
everyone has come to celebrate.

00:25:36.160 --> 00:25:41.040
It's for us Muslims and for all the Syrian people.

00:25:41.520 --> 00:25:44.960
Also for all the Sunni Muslims.

00:25:45.440 --> 00:25:51.760
For us Muslims, Friday is a day of rest,
a day of celebration. The regime deprived us of that..

00:25:51.920 --> 00:25:55.120
Of this very special day.
And now we're rid of him.

00:25:55.280 --> 00:25:59.680
Bashar al-Assad was a Muslim president,
he should have respected this day.

00:25:59.840 --> 00:26:03.760
But no, he had those who went to the mosque
to pray arrested and taken away.

00:26:03.920 --> 00:26:10.000
Just because they were going to pray. 3 quarters
of those who were arrested, it was because of that.

00:26:17.520 --> 00:26:20.240
The young woman has seen several of her relatives arrested,

00:26:20.640 --> 00:26:21.760
starting with her father.

00:26:22.440 --> 00:26:25.400
Her whole family lived in fear of being denounced.

00:26:28.720 --> 00:26:33.920
When the uprising started,
we all wanted to speak out.

00:26:34.080 --> 00:26:39.520
We were carried away by a feeling of freedom
and we realised just how silenced we had been.

00:26:39.680 --> 00:26:43.040
Even at home we were afraid to speak out.

00:26:43.200 --> 00:26:46.000
We were always saying that the walls had ears.

00:26:46.160 --> 00:26:49.760
It got to the point where we were even
afraid for our children,

00:26:49.920 --> 00:26:52.960
because even they could be targeted by the regime.

00:26:53.120 --> 00:26:55.200
They had no mercy.

00:26:55.600 --> 00:27:02.240
I'd like him to suffer as much as we did.
He deserves to be buried where he tortured his people.

00:27:03.160 --> 00:27:04.560
Now a stay-at-home mother,

00:27:04.880 --> 00:27:07.400
the beautician wants to believe in better days.

00:27:07.840 --> 00:27:09.760
We have hope.

00:27:09.920 --> 00:27:17.760
The people who liberated us told us:
"This is your country. We just want to pave the way".

00:27:17.920 --> 00:27:25.600
We are at the centre of their concerns,
they are helping us, they are very supportive.

00:27:25.840 --> 00:27:30.960
I think they want to raise our standard of living.

00:27:31.920 --> 00:27:33.480
The time for prayer is approaching.

00:27:34.160 --> 00:27:36.760
The young women return to the area around the mosque.

00:27:37.080 --> 00:27:40.760
Many of the people of Damascus have responded to the call of the HTS.

00:27:41.640 --> 00:27:43.280
This is more than a simple prayer.

00:27:43.840 --> 00:27:45.640
It's a gathering of an entire nation.

00:27:46.200 --> 00:27:48.760
The regime's new flags are flying everywhere.

00:27:49.120 --> 00:27:51.600
Ask where they got their flags.

00:27:51.760 --> 00:27:55.600
Look at the crowds around the mosque,
there's not going to be any more room.

00:27:56.040 --> 00:27:58.560
Razan was not expecting such a large crowd.

00:27:59.240 --> 00:28:00.200
The new prime minister,

00:28:00.360 --> 00:28:01.360
Mohammed al-Bashir,

00:28:01.680 --> 00:28:03.960
is due to give a speech during these prayers.

00:28:04.720 --> 00:28:09.400
So every Syrian wants to see and hear the man who was appointed by the new government.

00:28:13.360 --> 00:28:14.960
How do you feel?

00:28:15.200 --> 00:28:21.920
The feeling is indescribable. I'm overcome
with immense joy, we're very happy.

00:28:22.080 --> 00:28:26.000
We hope that everything will turn out
the way we want it to.

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:29.200
I'm afraid I'm dreaming, that it's all unreal.

00:28:29.360 --> 00:28:31.600
I'm really afraid I'm dreaming.

00:28:35.440 --> 00:28:42.640
Bashar al-Assad, the people want you executed!
Bashar al-Assad, the people want you executed!

00:28:42.800 --> 00:28:47.040
Bashar al-Assad, the people want you executed!

00:28:48.040 --> 00:28:53.840
This is the first time in modern Syrian history that a prime minister has addressed the nation from a mosque.

00:28:55.120 --> 00:29:02.880
We have done all this to establish a state of law,
a state of freedom,

00:29:03.360 --> 00:29:07.760
justice and dignity for all.

00:29:08.640 --> 00:29:12.320
We will protect the rights of all the poor in society.

00:29:12.480 --> 00:29:15.440
And we will restore dignity to all who have lost it.

00:29:16.520 --> 00:29:18.880
Still relatively unknown to the Syrian people,

00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:26.640
this engineer by training is tasked with overseeing the country's political transition until the 1st of March 2025.

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:29.000
Will the promises of freedom be kept?

00:29:29.560 --> 00:29:31.400
Especially for religious minorities.

00:29:32.160 --> 00:29:33.640
Not far from the main mosque,

00:29:33.800 --> 00:29:34.880
in the Christian quarter,

00:29:35.240 --> 00:29:38.800
the new government is welcomed with a mixture of joy and anxiety,

00:29:39.280 --> 00:29:40.480
as is the case with Tala.

00:29:41.440 --> 00:29:44.240
Hi Johnny, how are you?

00:29:45.280 --> 00:29:50.480
Can you and Sarah come and pick us up
so we can go shopping?

00:29:53.600 --> 00:29:56.920
She is about to go out with her sister Sarah and her friend Koko.

00:29:57.840 --> 00:29:59.840
Since the HTS took over the country,

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:03.640
The women in this Christian family have not gone out without a man.

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:07.680
Today it's their friend Johnny who'll be acting as chaperone.

00:30:14.680 --> 00:30:18.000
There were two million Christians in Syria before the civil war.

00:30:18.800 --> 00:30:21.640
Three-quarters have left the country since 2011.

00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:30.080
Honestly in the current situation, it's reassuring
if there's a friend with us

00:30:30.240 --> 00:30:33.040
because at the moment,
we don't know what can happen.

00:30:33.200 --> 00:30:36.880
Until everyone can live their lives as they used to.

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:44.960
I saw a man dressed in a tunic,
a beard and a hat, like an Afghan.

00:30:45.520 --> 00:30:49.600
A very big beard and another with his face covered.

00:30:50.560 --> 00:30:53.920
It has to be said that the members of HTS
look a bit scary.

00:30:54.480 --> 00:30:57.440
You mean physically?
- Yes, physically.

00:30:58.000 --> 00:31:02.800
We're not used to this. We've never seen
anything like it. Neither before nor after the crisis.

00:31:04.120 --> 00:31:05.480
They go to the supermarket.

00:31:08.320 --> 00:31:08.600
Tala,

00:31:08.920 --> 00:31:14.640
her sister Sarah and her friend Koko are stocking up because they're worried about what might happen next.

00:31:15.280 --> 00:31:17.240
There are rumours of shortages to come.

00:31:18.560 --> 00:31:22.800
Let's see what we need at home.

00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:26.680
In this local store run by a Muslim family,

00:31:27.120 --> 00:31:32.880
they freely express their fears about the fate that the country's new leaders may have in store for Syrian women.

00:31:34.960 --> 00:31:41.840
What worries me is the outbreak of a religious war,
or a civil war.

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:44.560
If he starts giving us instructions like

00:31:44.720 --> 00:31:50.720
"women, don't go out, don't work, cover up,
don't go out any more".

00:31:50.880 --> 00:31:54.080
we are afraid that there will be
no more individual freedom for women.

00:31:54.240 --> 00:31:59.680
That we won't be able to go to university,
that we won't be able to work, nothing at all.

00:31:59.840 --> 00:32:01.520
That's what we're afraid of.

00:32:02.920 --> 00:32:04.320
The shelves are fully stocked,

00:32:04.760 --> 00:32:05.640
but inflation,

00:32:05.880 --> 00:32:08.080
already high before the fall of the regime,

00:32:08.360 --> 00:32:09.400
is taking its toll.

00:32:10.120 --> 00:32:13.600
What's most striking is the absence of labels showing prices.

00:32:13.920 --> 00:32:17.520
Prices used to be displayed everywhere.

00:32:17.760 --> 00:32:18.080
Prices used to be displayed everywhere.

00:32:18.240 --> 00:32:18.960
Creme But now there aren't any.

00:32:19.120 --> 00:32:21.120
But now there aren't any.

00:32:21.280 --> 00:32:24.640
Prices change every day
depending on the value of the dollar.

00:32:24.800 --> 00:32:30.800
We don't even have a government
or a minister to regulate all that.

00:32:32.160 --> 00:32:32.640
The prices are determined.

00:32:32.640 --> 00:32:32.680
So,

00:32:32.680 --> 00:32:34.600
Tala learns the prices at the checkout.

00:32:36.240 --> 00:32:38.640
How much is the oil now? 2,000?

00:32:39.800 --> 00:32:40.440
For the moment,

00:32:40.560 --> 00:32:42.360
the price of oil has not changed.

00:32:43.120 --> 00:32:44.280
Nor have the banknotes,

00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:46.960
which still bear Bashar al-Assad's image.

00:32:50.240 --> 00:32:50.880
After shopping,

00:32:51.160 --> 00:32:54.360
the group of friends decide to stop for a bite to eat outside.

00:32:55.080 --> 00:32:55.320
Soon,

00:32:55.560 --> 00:32:56.760
the tension is palpable.

00:32:58.320 --> 00:33:00.800
Two dust-covered cars are parked behind them.

00:33:01.480 --> 00:33:02.800
They are armed rebels.

00:33:11.200 --> 00:33:15.520
I'm nervous. They're all there.

00:33:15.760 --> 00:33:16.880
Shall we go?

00:33:18.320 --> 00:33:18.440
The

00:33:18.480 --> 00:33:19.720
girls decide to leave.

00:33:20.520 --> 00:33:25.840
The reason that these jihadists frighten them is that everyone still remembers the Raqqa caliphate.

00:33:32.120 --> 00:33:37.120
It was in the town of Raqqa in the north of Syria that the Islamic State established its capital.

00:33:39.520 --> 00:33:42.240
From 2014 to 2017,

00:33:42.280 --> 00:33:47.080
ISIS imposed Sharia law at its harshest and committed the most terrible atrocities.

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:48.880
For many Syrians,

00:33:49.160 --> 00:33:52.200
while the jihadists may use one hand for social action,

00:33:52.800 --> 00:33:56.560
they are also capable of using the other to strike without mercy.

00:34:00.960 --> 00:34:02.680
The new strongman of Damascus,

00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:04.360
Abu Mohammed al-Julani,

00:34:04.920 --> 00:34:06.520
once close to the Islamic State,

00:34:07.040 --> 00:34:09.200
distanced himself from it in 2011.

00:34:10.040 --> 00:34:11.520
He's a chameleon-like figure.

00:34:12.240 --> 00:34:14.280
Who really is Syria's new leader?

00:34:15.400 --> 00:34:17.080
Meet journalist Wassim Nasser,

00:34:17.400 --> 00:34:19.880
the only expert on jihadism to have met him.

00:34:20.560 --> 00:34:23.280
When he was very young, in his early twenties,

00:34:23.440 --> 00:34:28.560
Jolani went to Iraq to fight against the American
armed forces as a member of al-Qaeda.

00:34:28.720 --> 00:34:32.880
He was sent by the late Baghdadi,
caliph of the Islamic State,

00:34:33.040 --> 00:34:36.640
to establish what has become the Nusra Front in Syria.

00:34:38.640 --> 00:34:43.600
He is on the list of terrorists wanted by the Americans,
with a 10 million price on his head.

00:34:45.720 --> 00:34:49.520
Mohamed Al-Jolani officially severed his ties with the Nusra Front,

00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:52.320
an Islamist group affiliated with Al-Qaeda.

00:34:55.560 --> 00:34:56.360
On the same day,

00:34:56.640 --> 00:34:57.920
he launched his own movement,

00:34:58.120 --> 00:34:59.520
Hayat Tahrir Al Sham

00:35:04.640 --> 00:35:10.560
We declare the complete cancellation of all operations
under the name of the Nusra Front.

00:35:10.720 --> 00:35:14.800
We are building a new group operating
under the name of Hayat Tahrir al-Sham.

00:35:14.960 --> 00:35:20.400
We affirm that this new organisation
is not affiliated to any outside entity.

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:30.320
The real clash was going to be with the Islamic State.

00:35:30.480 --> 00:35:38.000
There were pitched battles, hundreds of deaths
and that's when Jolani achieved independence.

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:40.960
Jolani has taken on a new image.

00:35:41.480 --> 00:35:45.760
He's changed his style of dress and no longer appears in a religious tunic.

00:35:46.400 --> 00:35:48.720
He sometimes even wears civilian clothes.

00:35:49.480 --> 00:35:52.760
He's mastered the strategy of communicating through style,

00:35:53.160 --> 00:35:53.920
often military.

00:35:54.800 --> 00:36:01.520
We're talking to anyone capable of bearing arms
or anyone capable of doing their duty as a jihadist.

00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:04.000
The time to fight is now.

00:36:05.520 --> 00:36:11.040
When I went to see Joulani in Idlib,
in mid-2023,

00:36:11.200 --> 00:36:16.000
I met a soldier but I also had the impression
that I was meeting a politician.

00:36:16.600 --> 00:36:18.680
In his conservative stronghold of Idlib,

00:36:18.840 --> 00:36:22.040
Mohamed Al-Julani has to deal with different groups of fighters.

00:36:22.280 --> 00:36:25.000
He now manages a city of 4 million inhabitants.

00:36:28.080 --> 00:36:29.920
It's not at all a Taliban-style system.

00:36:30.080 --> 00:36:35.200
Women have access to education.
So it's more the traditional Syrian code that applies.

00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:42.640
That doesn't make him a democrat or a liberal,
he's still a strict Islamist.

00:36:43.200 --> 00:36:47.920
We're prepared to die to keep our people safe.
That's our raison d'être.

00:36:53.280 --> 00:36:57.360
He came out of the global jihad and became
a player on the Syrian scene.

00:36:57.520 --> 00:37:02.800
He said to me "my objective is to retake Damascus
and topple Bashar al-Assad"

00:37:04.320 --> 00:37:07.120
And what he said to me was exactly what he then did.

00:37:07.600 --> 00:37:11.360
Our brothers in Homs, get ready,
we're coming to every town.

00:37:11.520 --> 00:37:15.120
Damascus, Deraa, Deir- ez-Zor.
We'll take them all, inshallah.

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:17.520
With just 20,000 men,

00:37:19.720 --> 00:37:25.120
Mohammed Al-Jolani has succeeded in toppling one of the Middle East's most bloodthirsty dictators.

00:37:26.080 --> 00:37:29.840
Will he be able to keep his distance from the supporters of an international jihad?

00:37:31.080 --> 00:37:31.600
Because,

00:37:31.800 --> 00:37:32.640
to take the country,

00:37:32.960 --> 00:37:36.800
the HTS brigades fought with independent jihadists at their side.

00:37:37.280 --> 00:37:38.200
Like this Frenchman,

00:37:38.440 --> 00:37:40.320
who filmed the stages of the conquest,

00:37:40.400 --> 00:37:44.320
Down with al-Assad.
Allahu Akbar!

00:37:45.280 --> 00:37:48.560
Today there are still around a hundred French people living in Syria.

00:37:49.120 --> 00:37:51.920
Even the Christians are happy.
Allahu Akbar.

00:37:56.400 --> 00:38:00.640
It's not easy to know how many of them took part in the offensive led by Jolani.

00:38:03.840 --> 00:38:08.720
Entry into the city of Latakia. Welcome from
the civilian population. Allahu Akbar.

00:38:13.960 --> 00:38:16.080
One of them has arranged to meet us in Idlib,

00:38:16.440 --> 00:38:18.160
a seven-hour drive from the capital.

00:38:19.120 --> 00:38:21.600
This is the stronghold of Jolani's HTS,

00:38:21.880 --> 00:38:23.120
his movement's laboratory,

00:38:23.560 --> 00:38:26.080
which could inspire the management of the new Syria.

00:38:27.080 --> 00:38:29.040
Compared with the other towns we passed through,

00:38:29.360 --> 00:38:30.720
this one seems better run.

00:38:31.320 --> 00:38:34.480
The market stalls are fully stocked and all the shops are open.

00:38:37.320 --> 00:38:39.240
The police are controlling the traffic.

00:38:46.600 --> 00:38:47.760
Unlike in Damascus,

00:38:48.040 --> 00:38:50.120
the women we see here are all veiled.

00:38:55.880 --> 00:38:56.720
This is Hicham,

00:38:57.080 --> 00:38:58.560
a French jihadist from Nice.

00:38:59.520 --> 00:39:01.320
His fighting name is Saifullah,

00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:03.160
literally Sword of God.

00:39:03.920 --> 00:39:08.200
There's a Kalashnikov slung across his back and magazines strapped to his chest.

00:39:09.040 --> 00:39:11.760
Although he knows that he's wanted by the French authorities,

00:39:12.120 --> 00:39:14.600
he agrees to testify with his face uncovered.

00:39:15.760 --> 00:39:17.200
Don't worry.

00:39:18.680 --> 00:39:20.720
Although he supports Jolani's offensive,

00:39:21.000 --> 00:39:24.800
he says he does not belong to HTS but is independent.

00:39:26.000 --> 00:39:29.840
The independents are called "mostakilin".

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:35.520
That's people who are independent but have
a good relationship with HTS.

00:39:36.000 --> 00:39:37.520
With everyone.

00:39:37.680 --> 00:39:40.960
Whether it's with civilians, with the free army
or with everyone else.

00:39:41.120 --> 00:39:46.800
So the control that there is here in the Idlib region,
Idlib is HTS.

00:39:46.960 --> 00:39:49.200
They control the territory.

00:39:49.360 --> 00:39:55.040
They have to govern by Sharia law, OK.
By divine law, not democratic law.

00:39:55.200 --> 00:39:59.440
So what's going to happen, and what's being said,
are two different things. We don't know.

00:40:00.320 --> 00:40:06.080
So Jolani's supporters are far from being completely on board with the official line of Syria's new master.

00:40:07.280 --> 00:40:12.000
Hisham says he arrived in Idlib eight years ago via Omar Omzan's network.

00:40:13.080 --> 00:40:15.480
This jihadist was one of the main French recruiters.

00:40:16.160 --> 00:40:18.200
He's said to have rallied around 50 men,

00:40:18.440 --> 00:40:20.000
all from Nice and the Côte d'Azur.

00:40:30.640 --> 00:40:34.400
This is a neighbour.
One of our neighbours.

00:40:35.840 --> 00:40:38.880
How are you, my friend?
How are you? It's been a while.

00:40:39.040 --> 00:40:41.920
I'm fine. I saw you from a distance.

00:40:42.480 --> 00:40:48.720
Those are our French friends. What do you think
of foreigners like me who have come here?

00:40:48.880 --> 00:40:54.000
Very good. They're our brothers.
We have a very good relationship.

00:40:54.160 --> 00:40:56.560
They're real brothers!

00:40:57.840 --> 00:41:00.160
Hisham heads towards Idlib city centre,

00:41:00.520 --> 00:41:02.320
passing through the outskirts of the city.

00:41:04.400 --> 00:41:06.240
That's the Idlib stadium.

00:41:06.400 --> 00:41:12.400
I think the World Cup will be here soon.
arsa, Messi or Ronaldo may come here. You never knov

00:41:13.600 --> 00:41:15.960
He is married here and started a second family.

00:41:16.800 --> 00:41:17.680
And for the Frenchman,

00:41:18.080 --> 00:41:20.040
everyday life seems almost normal.

00:41:20.080 --> 00:41:26.400
You have a vision of Syria, Hiroshima.

00:41:27.280 --> 00:41:30.880
It's true that there's war, but there's life.

00:41:31.200 --> 00:41:34.880
People need to live, they need to eat,
they need to work.

00:41:35.040 --> 00:41:41.520
Children need to go to sport and school like
everyone else, so there you have it.

00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:46.240
For example, my wife is a school teacher.
So I let her work.

00:41:46.560 --> 00:41:52.480
But I agree that my wife should go to work.
There's no problem with that.

00:41:52.720 --> 00:41:53.120
However,

00:41:53.400 --> 00:41:57.440
what he's saying is far from the line taken by Joulani and his lieutenants.

00:41:57.640 --> 00:42:00.320
Hisham wants the Syrians to follow the Afghan model.

00:42:00.680 --> 00:42:02.280
His ideal is the Taliban.

00:42:03.040 --> 00:42:09.360
In Afghanistan, they fought for 42 years,
sacrificing their lives and their time.

00:42:11.040 --> 00:42:15.680
They lived in fear, joy and famine.

00:42:16.240 --> 00:42:21.920
And they managed to take back
the whole of Afghanistan.

00:42:22.080 --> 00:42:26.400
And now they are living at home,
with their own rules. OK?

00:42:27.280 --> 00:42:31.600
And what a source of pride.
That's something to be proud of.

00:42:32.880 --> 00:42:35.360
The Frenchman may have rebuilt his life in Syria,

00:42:35.800 --> 00:42:37.840
but he left behind two children in Nice.

00:42:38.600 --> 00:42:40.720
Does he intend to return to France one day?

00:42:41.200 --> 00:42:42.560
I don't think so.

00:42:42.800 --> 00:42:50.640
First of all, I'm not interested in going back
and secondly, what's waiting for me

00:42:50.800 --> 00:42:55.600
won't be a hotel room or a cosy home.

00:42:55.760 --> 00:43:01.760
I think it will be prison,
so, to avoid that, I'm going to stay here.

00:43:05.200 --> 00:43:10.160
Will these jihadists scatter into thin air
because they have no place in this Syrian movement,

00:43:10.320 --> 00:43:13.520
as they themselves are not Syrians?

00:43:13.680 --> 00:43:21.440
Will they join the Islamic State cells that still exist,
as we know, in northern Syria and Iraq?

00:43:27.320 --> 00:43:28.960
as we know,

00:43:28.960 --> 00:43:31.160
in northern Syria and in Iraq?

00:43:31.360 --> 00:43:32.720
of the HTS brigades.

00:43:33.640 --> 00:43:34.640
We're heading for Aleppo,

00:43:35.120 --> 00:43:37.120
the first city conquered by Al-Julani.

00:43:38.040 --> 00:43:42.280
It came under rebel control after massive bombardment by the Russian air force.

00:43:49.480 --> 00:43:51.160
A jewel of Syrian culture,

00:43:51.600 --> 00:43:53.640
this is one of the oldest cities in the world.

00:43:54.200 --> 00:43:56.000
A UNESCO World Heritage Site,

00:43:56.280 --> 00:43:59.160
it has long been the country's main tourist destination.

00:44:00.120 --> 00:44:01.040
In the main square,

00:44:01.480 --> 00:44:04.240
life is returning to normal among the street vendors.

00:44:07.360 --> 00:44:10.080
3 packs of cakes for 10 euros

00:44:10.960 --> 00:44:11.200
Here,

00:44:11.360 --> 00:44:13.600
while the symbols of the past have been destroyed,

00:44:13.840 --> 00:44:14.680
others have appeared.

00:44:15.240 --> 00:44:16.360
Notably the new flag,

00:44:16.960 --> 00:44:19.200
flanked by three red stars on a green,

00:44:19.400 --> 00:44:20.600
white and black background.

00:44:21.680 --> 00:44:23.080
Now the flag of the revolution,

00:44:23.560 --> 00:44:27.160
it's been the symbol of the opposition since the civil war in 2011.

00:44:30.640 --> 00:44:31.480
On the billboards,

00:44:31.720 --> 00:44:36.240
members of HTS are already displaying their victory over this historic city.

00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:44.760
Abdelhaï Kadoué is an unmissable figure in Aleppo.

00:44:46.840 --> 00:44:51.480
This French-speaking shopkeeper and hotelier can't stop talking about his city.

00:44:52.160 --> 00:44:54.800
We're in the Bab Antakya souk.

00:44:54.960 --> 00:45:00.560
The entrance to the souks, the western entrance
to the souks of Aleppo.

00:45:00.560 --> 00:45:02.240
Aleppo?

00:45:02.480 --> 00:45:03.920
He wanders through this souk,

00:45:04.360 --> 00:45:06.280
the largest covered market in the world,

00:45:06.680 --> 00:45:09.080
a maze of 13 kilometres of alleyways.

00:45:09.920 --> 00:45:13.600
This thousand-year-old district is packed with architectural treasures.

00:45:14.320 --> 00:45:18.960
This was Aleppo's first mosque, in 1637.

00:45:19.120 --> 00:45:23.520
It was built on a triumphal arch from Roman times.

00:45:24.360 --> 00:45:26.480
Born near Aleppo 67 years ago,

00:45:27.080 --> 00:45:27.640
Abdel Hai...

00:45:28.000 --> 00:45:29.840
Like the majority of Syrians we meet,

00:45:30.320 --> 00:45:34.880
welcomes the fall of Bashir al-Assad's regime and hopes for lasting peace.

00:45:36.400 --> 00:45:42.000
I feel happy. I see that people have gone back
to their shops.

00:45:50.640 --> 00:45:52.880
And that life goes on.

00:45:53.280 --> 00:46:00.160
Life goes on. Even if there aren't many customers
in the souks, as you can see.

00:46:00.320 --> 00:46:07.280
it people have hope, and that's the most important thin
Hope for a better future.

00:46:08.480 --> 00:46:10.160
The deeper you go into the souk,

00:46:10.600 --> 00:46:12.680
the more you see the scars of the civil war,

00:46:13.560 --> 00:46:16.600
all the way to alleyways that have been completely destroyed.

00:46:17.440 --> 00:46:18.320
In 2011,

00:46:18.600 --> 00:46:25.240
rebels opposed to Bashar al-Assad's regime reportedly dynamited and bombed a large part of this historic site.

00:46:30.640 --> 00:46:36.640
The Syrians have a very strong desire
to rebuild the city.

00:46:38.080 --> 00:46:44.560
This was the most interesting part of the souk.
It was the spice souk.

00:46:44.800 --> 00:46:49.760
All the shops sold perfumes, spices,

00:46:49.920 --> 00:46:54.480
saffron and spices in general in this part of the souk.

00:46:54.640 --> 00:47:00.720
Insha'allah, you will come back and you will see,
now with this new period

00:47:01.360 --> 00:47:05.680
without corruption

00:47:05.840 --> 00:47:13.040
and with the help of the United Nations, the people
who adore our culture.

00:47:13.200 --> 00:47:16.320
It's going to happen soon.

00:47:17.360 --> 00:47:19.160
Abdelhai invites us to his home.

00:47:19.840 --> 00:47:22.800
He owns a traditional guest house in the old town of Aleppo.

00:47:27.320 --> 00:47:30.800
Decorated with Syrian antiques patiently collected over the years,

00:47:31.280 --> 00:47:34.960
it has long been a favourite haunt of tourists from all over the world.

00:47:35.440 --> 00:47:37.240
But it's now completely deserted.

00:47:39.200 --> 00:47:46.800
Before 2011, the five or six 5-star hotels in Aleppo
had around a thousand rooms

00:47:46.960 --> 00:47:50.000
and were always full.

00:47:50.640 --> 00:47:58.560
Generally all year round, all year round,
I mean all seasons, summer and winter,

00:47:58.720 --> 00:48:02.880
I had 90% occupancy.

00:48:04.720 --> 00:48:11.600
That means that 15 rooms were full all year round.

00:48:13.320 --> 00:48:17.000
15 rooms were full all year round.

00:48:18.880 --> 00:48:25.600
It's tolerant, there's calm.
We haven't seen any trouble.

00:48:25.840 --> 00:48:30.160
Will they change? I don't know.
For the moment it's fine.

00:48:30.320 --> 00:48:34.240
We need order, little by little.

00:48:34.400 --> 00:48:40.720
Because I don't know their members for the
administration. But they've left everyone alone.

00:48:40.880 --> 00:48:48.240
They've announced that everyone should go
ack to work. The schools are going to open next week

00:48:48.400 --> 00:48:54.000
The banks are already open
and next week they'll open again.

00:48:54.240 --> 00:49:00.240
And people's money is guaranteed in the banks.

00:49:00.400 --> 00:49:06.880
And that's something that reassures people
and is very important for the future.

00:49:17.240 --> 00:49:20.800
There were 200,000 Christians before the start of the Civil War.

00:49:21.280 --> 00:49:21.600
Today,

00:49:21.840 --> 00:49:23.160
there are just 30,000.

00:49:23.960 --> 00:49:25.000
There's no denying it.

00:49:25.360 --> 00:49:30.640
Eastern Christians have been targeted by the various Islamist factions that have clashed in the country.

00:49:31.800 --> 00:49:32.520
Bishop Jalouf,

00:49:32.920 --> 00:49:35.120
ordained as Apostolic Vicar by the Pope,

00:49:35.560 --> 00:49:38.800
is one of the Vatican's most eminent representatives in Syria.

00:49:39.160 --> 00:49:41.920
He himself was a victim of the jihadist rebels.

00:49:42.320 --> 00:49:48.240
There have been murders, repression, threats.

00:49:48.640 --> 00:49:54.720
Many Christians have been kidnapped
and had their houses and land seized.

00:49:54.880 --> 00:50:02.800
nyself have been kidnapped twice and put in prison onc
I have been the target of an assassination attempt.

00:50:03.720 --> 00:50:06.000
For 22 years he was a priest in Idlib,

00:50:06.160 --> 00:50:07.680
the stronghold of the HTS.

00:50:08.120 --> 00:50:10.480
Last year he asked to meet Syria's new leader.

00:50:10.960 --> 00:50:12.640
With Christmas just a few days away,

00:50:12.880 --> 00:50:15.280
he's very optimistic about Mohamed Al-Julani,

00:50:15.520 --> 00:50:17.960
who he believes will be able to unify the country.

00:50:18.960 --> 00:50:25.200
We saw him and presented him
with all our problems,

00:50:25.360 --> 00:50:29.600
difficulties and persecutions.

00:50:29.840 --> 00:50:36.000
Personally, I'm not afraid of the future. But the people
who have lived through the repression are very afraid.

00:50:36.160 --> 00:50:42.080
In recent months, the rebels have reassured us.

00:50:42.720 --> 00:50:48.240
They have told us that our situation
is not going to get any worse.

00:50:48.640 --> 00:50:55.680
They told us "We have not come to invade you,
but to help you live in dignity, in freedom,

00:50:55.840 --> 00:51:03.840
in a new democracy, free and sovereign,
where everyone's rights will be respected".

00:51:05.040 --> 00:51:05.600
SYRIA

00:51:05.720 --> 00:51:07.800
350 kilometres from Aleppo,

00:51:08.040 --> 00:51:09.200
in the capital Damascus,

00:51:09.520 --> 00:51:11.520
the curfew was lifted four days ago.

00:51:15.760 --> 00:51:16.640
In the main square,

00:51:17.000 --> 00:51:17.760
every evening,

00:51:18.040 --> 00:51:22.000
Syrians are taking the opportunity to celebrate this new page in their history.

00:51:26.520 --> 00:51:30.600
The jihadist rebels who used to inspire fear are now the country's new.

00:51:31.600 --> 00:51:36.240
It's a joy shared by all Syrians.

00:51:36.640 --> 00:51:41.600
We have got the result we wanted, thank God,
and we're going to move forward.

00:51:41.760 --> 00:51:49.040
I haven't been to Damascus for 14 years, 14 years,
because that pig Bashar deprived us of it.

00:51:56.880 --> 00:51:58.240
For young women like Razan,

00:51:58.400 --> 00:51:59.920
the beautician we met at the mosque,

00:52:00.240 --> 00:52:02.800
a united country finally seems possible.

00:52:04.880 --> 00:52:10.400
Come back, you children of our land.
This is your country. Come back and build it.

00:52:10.560 --> 00:52:12.000
Bring it your strength.

00:52:14.400 --> 00:52:15.840
Long live Syria!

00:52:16.680 --> 00:52:17.920
the young medical intern,

00:52:17.960 --> 00:52:22.400
is also here to share in this historic moment of renewed unity among Syrians.

00:52:23.320 --> 00:52:25.440
People are indeed celebrating from their hearts.

00:52:25.920 --> 00:52:26.160
You know,

00:52:26.200 --> 00:52:27.360
it's not just like before,

00:52:27.680 --> 00:52:28.520
just fake smiles,

00:52:28.960 --> 00:52:31.080
being pushed and forced to just,

00:52:31.160 --> 00:52:31.400
you know,

00:52:31.400 --> 00:52:31.880
celebrate.

00:52:32.400 --> 00:52:33.680
Now people are being happy.

00:52:34.520 --> 00:52:35.760
Syria has entered a new,

00:52:35.920 --> 00:52:37.200
very uncertain era.

00:52:37.640 --> 00:52:41.000
The country is now hanging onto its destiny by a thread.

